.TH smi-half-past-run "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Base Command"
.SH NAME
smi-half-past-run \- Run the half past plugins, at half past every hour
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-half-past-run
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-half-past-run
runs every executable
.B .sh
plugin in the
.B half-past
directory of the setmy.info lib directory,
.I /opt/setmy.info/lib/half-past
in an installed package, one after another, without arguments.
It is the time based counterpart of
.BR smi-incoming-deploy (1),
which runs its plugins on file system events.
.PP
Plugins run in the byte order of their file names, sorted in the C locale whatever the system
language is. Prefix the names with two digits to set the order:
.BR 00_ ,
.BR 10_ ,
.BR 20_ ,
and so on, leaving gaps so a plugin can be put in between later.
A file that is not executable is skipped.
.PP
A failing plugin does not stop the others: its name is reported on standard error, the
remaining plugins still run, and the command exits with 1 at the end so the systemd service
shows the failure.
A missing plugin directory is not an error.
.PP
The directory holding the command itself is put first on
.BR PATH ,
so plugins can call the other setmy.info commands by name, such as
.BR smi-var-location (1),
also when started by systemd, whose
.B PATH
does not contain it.
.SH TIMER
.PP
The package installs
.B setmy-info-half-past.timer
and
.BR setmy-info-half-past.service ,
linked into
.I /etc/systemd/system
and enabled by the rpm and deb install scripts.
The timer starts the service at half past every hour, 00:30, 01:30, 02:30 and so on, once an hour,
and once one minute after
it is activated, at installation and at every boot.
The service runs
.B smi-half-past-run
as root, after the network is online.
.PP
.RS
.nf
systemctl list-timers setmy-info-half-past.timer
journalctl -u setmy-info-half-past.service
.fi
.RE
.SH PLUGINS
.PP
Plugins shipped with the package, from
.I src/main/sh/lib/half-past
in the sources; every executable
.B .sh
file placed there is built and installed into
.I lib/half-past
without further changes:
.TP
.I 10_external-ip.sh
Writes the external Internet IP address to
.B ip.txt
in the directory
.BR smi-var-location (1)
prints, with
.BR smi-external-ip (1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/setmy.info/lib/half-past
Half past plugins, executable
.B .sh
files.
.TP
.I /opt/setmy.info/etc/systemd/system/setmy-info-half-past.timer
.TQ
.I /opt/setmy.info/etc/systemd/system/setmy-info-half-past.service
The timer and the service it starts.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every plugin succeeded, or there was nothing to run.
.TP
.B 1
At least one plugin failed.
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
Command written by Imre Tabur.
.SH "REPORTING BUGS"
.PP
Report smi-half-past-run bugs to \fIinfo@setmy.info\fR
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
